nio: skip DWC3 soft reset in the bulk gadget (it wedges the boot)

The bulk-console rebuild (662-664) dropped the skip-soft-reset fix from 654/655
and restored dwc_wr(DCTL, DCTL_CSFTRST). That write wedges this board: the
gadget thread hangs before the VBUS override, so the host never sees a device.
Configure endpoints on the state ABL left behind, as sweet 0074 does.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/nio_usb.c b/bsd/dev/nio_usb.c
--- a/bsd/dev/nio_usb.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/nio_usb.c
@@ -514,16 +514,19 @@
 	ud.dma_pa = ptoa_64(pn);
 
 	/* Device controller soft reset (PHY and global setup stay as ABL left them). */
+#if 0
+	/* nio: DCTL.CSFTRST wedges this board (654); the bulk rebuild (662-664)
+	 * restored it by dropping the skip. ABL already left the controller in
+	 * device mode with clocks on -- do not reset it. */
 	dwc_wr(DCTL, DCTL_CSFTRST);
 	int i;
 	for (i = 0; i < 500 && (dwc_rd(DCTL) & DCTL_CSFTRST); i++) {
 		delay(1000);
 	}
+#endif
+	int i = 0;
 	printf("nio: USB: soft reset %s after %d ms, GCTL 0x%08x DCFG 0x%08x\n",
-	    (dwc_rd(DCTL) & DCTL_CSFTRST) ? "STUCK" : "done", i, dwc_rd(GCTL), dwc_rd(DCFG));
-	if (dwc_rd(DCTL) & DCTL_CSFTRST) {
-		return;
-	}
+	    "skipped", i, dwc_rd(GCTL), dwc_rd(DCFG));
 
 	dwc_wr(GEVNTADRLO, (uint32_t)(ud.dma_pa + UD_EVT));
 	dwc_wr(GEVNTADRHI, (uint32_t)((ud.dma_pa + UD_EVT) >> 32));
